        <Document ID="F88E94D4-CAC9-4E5D-85F0-B8A4FFD8C03C">
            <Title>The Ghost</Title>
            <Text>The Ghost  Description
The ghost of Hamlet's father
Notes
The ghost of Hamlet's father who returns to tell his son that he was murdered by Claudius so that Claudius could assume the throne. He wants Hamlet to avenge him. The character is ambiguous—Hamlet wonders if the ghost is a demon trying to deceive him—and there is no definitive resolution in the play to what causes the ghost to appear.
Role
Protagonist's Father
Motivation
To warn his son of the fact that his uncle murdered him, and to challenge him to seek vengence for his death.
Gender
Male
Fatal Flaws
Too trusting of his brother
Inner Conflict
Wants his son to kill his brother to restore his honor
How They Die
Poisoned in the ear while sleeping in a garden
Characters That Die
No
Tags
STAGE: Exposition, STAGE: Falling Action, Foreshadowing, THEME: Mortality, THEME: Revenge, THEME: Religion, THEME: Corruption, THEME: Health of the Nation, Character Death
Category
Other
</Text>
