        <Document ID="3C5CAE5B-25AE-4230-8E27-F561FA1F1D3A">
            <Title>Hamlet</Title>
            <Text>Hamlet  Description
Prince of Denmark
Notes
The title character, Hamlet is the 30 year old Prince of Denmark, nephew to King Claudius, and son of Queen Gertrude. He hates his uncle and resents his mother. Studied at the University of Wittenberg, he is a thoughtful and melancholy individual, but who often makes impulsive, rash decisions. 
Role
Protagonist
Motivation
Hamlet seeks to get revenge for his father's death
Gender
Male
Fatal Flaws
Too melancholy, acts before thinking it through
Inner Conflict
Wants to take his own life AND get revenge for his father's murder
How They Die
Cut with a poisoned sword in a duel with Laertes
Attended Wittenberg
Yes
Royal Family Member
Yes
Characters That Die
Yes
Tags
STAGE: Exposition, STAGE: Rising Action, STAGE: Climax, STAGE: Falling Action, STAGE: Resolution, THEME: Mortality, THEME: Revenge, THEME: Madness, Character Death
Category
Main
</Text>
