        <Document ID="C98FB962-A614-4049-B9D2-C39F4B8D3396">
            <Title>Ophelia</Title>
            <Text>Ophelia  Description
Hamlet's love interest
Notes
Ophelia is the daughter of Polonius, sister to Laertes, and the woman that Hamlet is in love with. She's a sweet girl but who depends on the men around her to tell her what to do, and ultimately, it leads to her untimely death. She eventually goes mad and dies by falling in a river.
Motivation
Be a good daughter and sister
Gender
Female
Fatal Flaws
Relies too much on others
Inner Conflict
Wants to be with Hamlet, but doesn't want to defy her father
How They Die
Falls into a river and drowns
